# Implement workpad three-axis Review feedback

Before exiting an `/implement` Pi session (harness moves the issue to In Review after green checks), the existing Linear workpad comment (`## Agent Workpad`) **must** include a `### Review feedback` section with **exactly three** axis lines:

```markdown
### Review feedback

- Spec: (none)
- Standards: (none)
- Slop: (none)
```

Replace `(none)` with a finding when the parent self-review finds a miss (`- Spec: …`, `- Standards: …`, `- Slop/ …` for hard Slop). Never omit an axis. Never use bare `- (none)` or a single meta line.

Factory-checker replaces this block after `/code-review`; an empty or axis-less section causes a mechanical checker fail (`reviewFeedbackMissingSlopAxis`). Tighten only — see `docs/agents/error-ratcheting.md` (KIT-136).
